## Logging

Axum and Fastly entrypoints delegate logging to the reusable adapter runners;
do not initialize a second CLI logger before a runtime runner. Ordinary levels
come from `EDGEZERO__LOGGING__LEVEL` (Fastly reads its runtime Config Store), with
`Info` as the absent/invalid fallback. Managed boot warnings use `edgezero::boot`
at `Warn`, independently of ordinary `Error` or `Off`.

Cloudflare and Spin logger initializers are no-ops, not Rust facade backends.
To own logging on any target, set `owns_logging = true` in `app!`, install your
backend before entering the runner, and configure both backend and facade filters.
Reuse `edgezero_core::resolve_logging_level(&EnvConfig)`, `BOOT_LOG_TARGET`, and
`BOOT_LOG_LEVEL`; raising only `log::set_max_level` cannot restore backend-filtered
messages. No logging implementation is duplicated in the generated entrypoints.

